{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101","id":161866,"title":"Abomination 101","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-07T11:04:44-07:00","id":161866,"title":"Abomination 101","content":"I have a much better understanding of Vampire than Werewolf but there is a NPC in one game who is an Abomination and he needs stats. What are some important things to keep in mind? Also what is going on with the Gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T11:57:21-07:00","id":161893,"title":"","content":"Without access to the books at the moment, IIRC their Gnosis remains initially unchanged but cannot ever be increased. Also, it can slowly decrease over time if they act in &quot;un-Gaian&quot; fashion (like a vampire losing Humanity). I think their Gifts still work, except for Gifts which require them to directly interact with Spirits (they're snubbed for the most part, I think?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T11:58:05-07:00","id":161895,"title":"","content":"I should point out, I was talking about Permanent Gnosis, not Temporary Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:09:20-07:00","id":161908,"title":"","content":"So they can regain temporary losses? Like from using powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:12:56-07:00","id":161911,"title":"","content":"- A Garou who is embraced becomes the clan of its sire (or potentially Caitiff, as usual). He develops three dots in Disciplines appropriately, and inherits the clan Weakness.<br /> <br /> - <i>Technically</i> he becomes ronin; the tribe and totem refuse to acknowledge him (Except as an enemy, of course.) This means he loses the powers of Pure Greed, probably loses his tribal weakness (maybe not?) and cannot gain rank or renown. The exception is if the Abomination was a Black Spiral Dancer, and even then they are fairly despised.<br /> <br /> - The abomination can shapeshift to all five forms normally, and they function identically.<br /> <br /> - The Abomination retains its vulnerability to silver, gains an allergy to sunlight, and can treat assorted other forms of damage as a vampire does (Bashing is halved, electrical damage is no problem, etc)<br /> <br /> - Abominations cannot regenerate as Garou do. They can only &quot;naturally&quot; heal by spending Blood<br /> <br /> - The abomination has a blood pool appropriate to his Generation, and may spend blood the same as any other vampire - increasing attributes, mimicking body functions, healing, powering Disciplines, etc.<br /> <br /> - an Abomination retains its knowledge of all Gifts and rites it knew before the Embrace, and could theoretically teach them to other Garou. However, unless he entreats banes, his rites will not work for him. His Gifts are by default functional, though there may be exceptions - hard to imagine a silver Fang abomination would be able to use Wrath of Gaia, for instance.They cannot learn new Gifts, unless taught by banes or other Garou<br /> <br /> - The Abomination retains his Rage score, and can use Rage points normally.Abominations do not have Self-Control scores, and for them, Frenzy works just like it does for other Garou (including difficulties being based on moon phases.) House rule - an Abomination's effective Self-Control score is equal to (10 - Rage) / 2<br /> <br /> - The Abomination lacks a Courage trait as well, instead using Willpower in its place. No conversion here, werewolves are simply badass enough to have big ratings.<br /> <br /> - An abomination has never been human - they do not have a Humanity score. Instead they utilize their Gnosis score as a morality trait, in addition to its regular uses. it functions as Humanity, determining torpor length, dice pools during the day, blood costs for appearing alive, etc.<br /> <br /> - Abominations lack a Conscience trait. Instead when they commit a sin against gnosis, they roll gnosis at difficulty 7 (or higher, for egregious offenses). if they fail the roll, they lose a permanant point of gnosis. When a roll needs Conscience, utilize Gnosis - As with willpower, Garou are just cool enough to have big scores there.<br /> <br /> - Upon the embrace, all fetishes attuned to the Garou are freed. The abomination may attempt to re-attune them to himself, but the difficulty is 10, and a botch strips away a permanent point of Gnosis. if his gnosis is 6 or higher, it is also a violation of Gnostic morality, and calls for a check.<br /> <br /> - An abomination cannot spend experience to increase / regain lost Gnosis. Once it's gone, it's gone for good.<br /> <br /> - Abominations exist in a state of permanant harano - this is a semi-supernatural state of depression, where a garou realizes - and <i>embraces</i> the futility of existence as a garou. A character suffering harano must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) every scene to function normally; failure means that all of his dice pools are halved for that scene. he may spend a point of Willpower to overcome this for a scene. Unlike other Garou, an Abomination has no hope of alleviating this condition.<br /> <br /> - ...Except selling itself wholly and willingly to the Wyrm. In effect, this palces the Abomination wholly in the thrall of the Wyrm (or at least a very powerful Wyrm minion?) removing the burden of Harano, as well as preventing Gnosis degeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:18:32-07:00","id":161913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101?p=161911#post161911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A Garou who is embraced becomes the clan of its sire (or potentially Caitiff, as usual). He develops three dots in Disciplines appropriately, and inherits the clan Weakness.<br /> <br /> - <i>Technically</i> he becomes ronin; the tribe and totem refuse to acknowledge him (Except as an enemy, of course.) This means he loses the powers of Pure Greed, probably loses his tribal weakness (maybe not?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you even use tribal weaknesses. They're rather removed from basic play materials, and often seem like an arbitrary thing that was tacked on to force some kind of symmetry with Vampire's clan weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - an Abomination retains its knowledge of all Gifts and rites it knew before the Embrace, and could theoretically teach them to other Garou. However, unless he entreats banes, his rites will not work for him. His Gifts are by default functional, though there may be exceptions - hard to imagine a silver Fang abomination would be able to use Wrath of Gaia, for instance.. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Halo of the OH FUCK WHY DID I DO THAT?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:39:52-07:00","id":161962,"title":"","content":"Excellent description, TCCB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T18:15:09-07:00","id":162058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101?p=161911#post161911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <br /> <br /> - An abomination cannot spend experience to increase / regain lost Gnosis. Once it's gone, it's gone for good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean once used it doesn't come back or once lost through degeneration is cant return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T20:56:34-07:00","id":162172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BellaFeylin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101?p=162058#post162058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does this mean once used it doesn't come back or once lost through degeneration is cant return?</div> </div> </div> </div>An abomination can regain Gnosis <i>points</i> that it spends, through the usual ways - meditation, negotiating with (or eating) spirits, or - heaven forbid - obsorbing Gnosis from an opened caern.<br /> <br /> However, their Gnosis <i>rating</i> - the permanent points - are what get los for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:42:23-07:00","id":169952,"title":"","content":"Instead of the rules for violating/losing/gaining Humanity, they follow the Garou Litany. Note that includes &quot;Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans.&quot; Depending on how strictly the ST interprets that, it could include every feeding from any human (or ghoul, or wolf, or werewolf).<br /> <br /> Instead of losing Humanity, they lose Gnosis.<br /> <br /> I'd rule that some Gifts stop working. Some Gifts don't work for fallen shapeshifters (like Mother's Touch). A quick-and-dirty rule of thumb might be anything with Gaia, Wyld, Luna, or a tribal totem in or referenced by the name.<br /> <br /> Can't spend Blood Points in the same turn as Rage or Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Permanent Harano only sets in at less than 7 permanent Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Once they hit 0 Gnosis, in addition to presumably becoming a Wight they also can't step sideways, use Gifts or fetishes.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;Path&quot; of being a slave to the Wyrm I'd guess they have to follow the Dark Litany (pre-W20 Black Spiral Dancer Litany) to avoid losing Gnosis. In any case it loses free will to disobey whatever the Wyrm demands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-15-2014, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T08:10:20-07:00","id":177019,"title":"","content":"Okay so we have a Prince 5th gen from 500 CE who was once a SilverFang turned Brujah. I have one last question. Should an abomination drink from a werewolf would it cause frenzy check? (I was thinking it wouldn't be a gnosis check because we were specifically talking about a black spiral dancer being the blood source.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T08:22:58-07:00","id":177068,"title":"","content":"I doubt drinking Garou blood would do anything odd to a Garou, seeing as they are kind of... I don't know, &quot;used to it&quot;? Though, Abominations make terrible NPCs (and even worse PCs) due to the fact their system for maintaining their Gnosis (which is basically their Humanity now) is so strict and so easy to lose, and cannot be bought back, that they don't last long. If you have an Ancient Abomination running around, it has probably found a way to deal with the losing Gnosis issue. Which probably comes at a terrible cost... either service to the Wyrm or some sort of Demonic entity (like Demons). Hell (no pun intended), the Demons from Demon the Fallen (or Devil's Due, depending on ST Fiat) could probably act as a sort of Totem and patron spirit to the Abomination, keeping their Gnosis from fading. That or they develop some sort of Wyrm-ish Rite that lets them steal Gnosis from other Garou by devouring them. Just saying, it isn't going to be pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:17:16-07:00","id":177149,"title":"","content":"Actually, drinking Garou blood is cannibalism and DOES require a check...Unless his gnosis is 2 or lower<br /> <br /> And Garou blood does the same thing for an Abomination as it does any other vampire - lowered difficulty to frenzy, but boosted stats if it's pure-breed blood. And remember that Garou all have 25 blood points, regardless of form, due to their natural vitality.<br /> <br /> Also... this thing's a prince? The mind boggles! I guess it could work in Dark Ages, but it's kinda unlikely the Camarilla would allow an inhuman monster that worships demons and flips his crap at EVERYTHING (he has difficulty 2 to frenzy for several days of every month! 1, if he's Ahroun...) to sit as prince... and the Camarilla has plenty of people who could tear this guy to dead werewolf confetti, 5th generation or not.<br /> <br /> Of course if it's a straight werewolf game where Vampires are just evil bloodsucker, more power to you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:26:07-07:00","id":177158,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a 5th gen Garou Brujah fight Karsh. I wonder who'd win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:29:01-07:00","id":177160,"title":"","content":"There is a mutal blood bound involved and plot hooks for some post gehenna stuff stemming from him and a few other sorces. We are trying to keep him as close to the book excepting the gnosis/humanity issue. We are saying it is a 1st gen (or older) vampire assisting him and his blood bounded partner (who is just an old Malk). I am trying to get everything else right. He is an NPC I inheirtied from a different game without as much statted. It is going to involve a modified thing to do with Dementation and him being a Silver fang and being mutually bound to a Malk. Thier minds are merging and that is keeping him in check. The Malk in question is still got very high humanity. We are using them as tools for end of times.Also it is a territory on the edge of sabbat controled territory so he is allowed to exist as cannon fodder and as a wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","user":"BellaFeylin","date":".  adding a point 06-22-2014, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T13:38:42-07:00","id":177304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BellaFeylin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101?p=177019#post177019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so we have a Prince 5th gen from 500 CE who was once a SilverFang turned Brujah. I have one last question. Should an abomination drink from a werewolf would it cause frenzy check? (I was thinking it wouldn't be a gnosis check because we were specifically talking about a black spiral dancer being the blood source.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the usual lifespan for Abominations is measured in <i>days</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T18:08:17-07:00","id":177505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BellaFeylin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161866-abomination-101?p=177160#post177160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Also it is a territory on the edge of sabbat controled territory so he is allowed to exist as cannon fodder and as a wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>How secret is the Abomonation's Generation? If the Sabbat learn he's 5th gen, his vitae is an extremely tempting target, even if he is a whirling death machine in a fight. I can easily see a Bishop who's sick of the looming threat call in a War Party* on someone like that.<br /> <br /> *If you're not super familiar with Sabbat internals, a War Party is ritual hunt of an elder vampire who's an enemy to the Sabbat. One or more packs are assembled, told as much or as little about the target as their superior may know or feel like divulging, and sent to kill the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T06:42:43-07:00","id":178864,"title":"","content":"Sorta, most people, that have met him, know he is lower gen but not 5th, like 6th or 7th. The Cam isn't totally stupid there is a former Justicar and a few of her closest former archons in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1665-bellafeylin","name":"BellaFeylin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}